        "original_id": "7dde55b9-0106-5a1d-ba7c-355d4691d121",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Shame of a City, Unchained Memories, Fastpitch, Tigre Hill\n- People: Juliet Weber\n- Organizations: Philadelphia Film Festival, Federal Writers' Project\n- Systems: WPA Slave Narrative Collection\n- Topics: documentary films\n\nFacts:\n- Fastpitch is a film that Juliet Weber co-produced in 2000.\n- Unchained Memories is a 2003 documentary film about stories of former slaves who were interviewed during the 1930s as part of the Federal Writers' Project and preserved in the WPA Slave Narrative Collection.\n- Juliet Weber co-produced Unchained Memories in 2003.\n- The Shame of a City is a 2006 feature-length documentary that premiered at the Philadelphia Film Festival.\n- Tigre Hill is perhaps best known for his first documentary, The Shame of a City.",
